---
/**
 * Track 8 (Visual Math: Calculus), Lesson 4, illustration 1 of 2.
 *
 * The unit circle as the home of trig. A point on the unit circle at
 * angle x (counted counter-clockwise from the positive x-axis) sits at
 * (cos x, sin x). The picture marks the angle, draws the radius out to
 * the point, and drops the two perpendicular projections onto the axes
 * to read off cos x along the horizontal and sin x along the vertical.
 */

const cx = 280;
const cy = 195;
const R_UNIT = 120; // pixels per unit (radius of the unit circle in svg space)

const xAngleDeg = 60;
const xRad = (xAngleDeg * Math.PI) / 180;
const cosX = Math.cos(xRad);
const sinX = Math.sin(xRad);

const ptX = cx + cosX * R_UNIT;
const ptY = cy - sinX * R_UNIT;

const TEAL = '#0d9488';
const AMBER = '#d97706';
const ACCENT = '#7c3aed';

// arc for the angle marker (small arc at origin)
const ARC_R = 28;
const arcEndX = cx + ARC_R * Math.cos(xRad);
const arcEndY = cy - ARC_R * Math.sin(xRad);
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 740 360" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="ca-uccs-title ca-uccs-desc">
		<title id="ca-uccs-title">The unit circle with the point at angle x labeled (cos x, sin x)</title>
		<desc id="ca-uccs-desc">A two-dimensional coordinate scene with x and y axes through a central origin. A unit circle of radius one is drawn around the origin. A purple radius line runs from the origin to a point on the circle at angle x equals 60 degrees from the positive x-axis. The angle is marked with a small accent purple arc near the origin and labeled x. The point on the circle is labeled (cos x, sin x). A teal dashed segment drops from the point straight down to the horizontal axis, where the foot is labeled cos x. An amber dashed segment runs from the point straight left to the vertical axis, where the foot is labeled sin x.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="ca-uccs-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor" />
			</marker>
		</defs>

		{/* axes */}
		<line x1={cx - R_UNIT - 30} y1={cy} x2={cx + R_UNIT + 30} y2={cy} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" opacity="0.55" marker-end="url(#ca-uccs-arrow)" />
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy + R_UNIT + 30} x2={cx} y2={cy - R_UNIT - 30} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" opacity="0.55" marker-end="url(#ca-uccs-arrow)" />
		<text x={cx + R_UNIT + 36} y={cy + 4} font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">x-axis</text>
		<text x={cx + 6} y={cy - R_UNIT - 32} font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">y-axis</text>

		{/* unit circle */}
		<circle cx={cx} cy={cy} r={R_UNIT} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" opacity="0.5" />

		{/* angle arc */}
		<path d={`M ${cx + ARC_R} ${cy} A ${ARC_R} ${ARC_R} 0 0 0 ${arcEndX.toFixed(1)} ${arcEndY.toFixed(1)}`} fill="none" stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="1.6" />
		<text x={cx + ARC_R + 6} y={cy - 6} font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>x</text>

		{/* projections (dashed): cosX horizontal projection, sinX vertical projection */}
		<line x1={ptX} y1={ptY} x2={ptX} y2={cy} stroke={TEAL} stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 4" opacity="0.75" />
		<line x1={ptX} y1={ptY} x2={cx} y2={ptY} stroke={AMBER} stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="5 4" opacity="0.75" />

		{/* radius (purple bold line) */}
		<line x1={cx} y1={cy} x2={ptX} y2={ptY} stroke={ACCENT} stroke-width="2.6" />

		{/* the point */}
		<circle cx={ptX} cy={ptY} r="5" fill={ACCENT} />

		{/* labels */}
		<text x={ptX + 8} y={ptY - 8} font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>(cos x, sin x)</text>

		{/* cos x label along horizontal projection foot */}
		<text x={cx + (ptX - cx) / 2} y={cy + 22} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={TEAL}>cos x</text>

		{/* sin x label along vertical projection foot */}
		<text x={cx - 12} y={cy + (ptY - cy) / 2 + 4} text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill={AMBER}>sin x</text>

		<circle cx={cx} cy={cy} r="3" fill="currentColor" />

		{/* legend */}
		<g transform="translate(520, 100)">
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="160" rx="6" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.04" />
			<rect x="0" y="0" width="200" height="160" rx="6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.8" opacity="0.3" />
			<text x="100" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">at angle x:</text>
			<text x="100" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill={TEAL} font-weight="700">cos x = horizontal</text>
			<text x="100" y="78" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" fill={AMBER} font-weight="700">sin x = vertical</text>
			<text x="100" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="10" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.65">point lies on the unit circle:</text>
			<text x="100" y="136" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill={ACCENT}>cos²x + sin²x = 1</text>
		</g>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>The unit circle is where cos and sin live. Walk an angle x counter-clockwise from the positive x-axis; you land at the point (cos x, sin x). The two coordinates are exactly the horizontal and vertical legs of the radius triangle: read cos x off the x-axis, sin x off the y-axis. That single picture organizes every trig identity.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 740px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
